  "scientific_conclusion": "RF vs rules agreement rate on test set: 99.2%. RF accuracy vs rule-derived GT: 99.2%. Rules-only accuracy (definitional ceiling): 100.0%. The RF model was trained on data generated by the SAME safety rules. Agreement near 100% is expected \u2014 the RF has learned to reproduce the rules accurately. RF achieves 0.9911 macro-F1 vs rules ceiling of 1.0000. Key additional value RF provides beyond the rules: (1) a calibrated probability estimate (confidence) that the hard rules cannot produce; (2) potential generalisation to combinations of borderline features not captured by strict thresholds. The 15 disagreement cases are the margin where RF can differ from rule-direct application. HONEST ASSESSMENT: On simulation data, the RF classifier is largely a re-implementation of the safety rules. Its primary incremental value is the probability output (confidence score), not a fundamentally different prediction. This is expected when training data is rule-generated.",
